+## Response deadlines (optional rollout)
+
+With `DUE_TIMES=on`, all ticket objects include `due`, an ISO timestamp fixed from creation time and priority. Patching priority never changes it. `GET /tickets?overdue=true` lists only open and in-progress tickets strictly past this timestamp. This filter combines with status, priority, assignee, limit, and cursor. `overdue=false` leaves the list unrestricted; other values return the usual 400 error envelope. With the feature off, ticket responses omit `due` and the overdue query parameter is ignored as before.
